{
 "esm": "1.2.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "ifelse_mixed_whole_dynamic",
  "description": "An observed with NO declared shape defined by an `ifelse` whose condition is a runtime SCALAR, one branch an array over a declared index set and the other a scalar (`X = ifelse(lev < 2, F*2, 0.0)`, the NEI2016 emission observeds, issue #664). The observed takes its array branch's shape whichever branch is taken, so the scalar branch fills every element: condition true, false, scalar branch first, the `ifelse` inside elementwise arithmetic, and (dynamic variant) flipping during the run on a state. Dynamic variant: the same rules beside a state whose right-hand side gathers them, so they are lowered on the run-time path.",
  "authors": [
   "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
  ],
  "tags": [
   "native",
   "conformance"
  ]
 },
 "index_sets": {
  "cell": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": 3
  }
 },
